Why Was Memoization Created?

Imagine:

function square(num){
    return num * num;
}

Calling:

square(5);
square(5);
square(5);
square(5);

calculates every time.

For simple functions it's okay.

But for expensive operations like:

Fibonacci
Factorial
API Calls
Database Queries
Complex Calculations

recalculating wastes:

CPU
Time
Memory

So memoization was introduced.